3. Correctly handles nested MappingNodes by recursively merging their values
4. Preserves the YAML tags and node types in the merged result
5. Implements the "last value wins" behavior for non-MappingNode collisions
6. Returns the result in the expected format as a list of tuples

The code now properly handles the example case from the docstring where retention configurations are merged, with the keep_daily value being overwritten by the last occurrence (5) while preserving the keep_hourly value (24) from the first configuration.

