<repaired_code>
import requests
import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET
from urllib.parse import quote

def retrieve_and_parse_diaspora_webfinger(handle):
    """Retrieve and parse a remote Diaspora webfinger document."""
    try:
        # Split handle into username and domain
        if '@' not in handle:
            raise ValueError("Invalid handle format - must contain @")
            
        username, domain = handle.split('@', 1)
        if not username or not domain:
            raise ValueError("Invalid handle format")

        # Construct proper webfinger URL with the actual domain
        url = f"https://{domain}/.well-known/webfinger?resource=acct:{quote(handle)}"
        
        # Make request with timeout and error handling
        response = requests.get(url, timeout=10)
        response.raise_for_status()
        xml_data = response.content
        
        webfinger_data = {}
        
        root = ET.fromstring(xml_data)
        for child in root.iter():
            if child.tag == "{http://docs.oasis-open.org/ns/xri/xrd-1.0}Alias":
                webfinger_data["alias"] = child.text
            elif child.tag == "{http://docs.oasis-open.org/ns/xri/xrd-1.0}Link":
                rel = child.attrib.get("rel")
                if rel == "http://webfinger.net/rel/profile-page":
                    webfinger_data["profile_page"] = child.attrib.get("href")
                elif rel == "http://schemas.google.com/g/2010#updates-from":
                    webfinger_data["updates_from"] = child.attrib.get("href")
        
        return webfinger_data
        
    except requests.exceptions.RequestException as e:
        raise ConnectionError(f"Failed to retrieve webfinger document: {str(e)}")
    except ET.ParseError as e:
        raise ValueError(f"Invalid XML data received: {str(e)}")
    except Exception as e:
        raise RuntimeError(f"Unexpected error while processing webfinger: {str(e)}")
</repaired_code>

The key improvements made:
1. Added proper handle parsing to extract domain
2. Used urllib.parse.quote to properly encode the handle in URL
3. Added comprehensive error handling for network, parsing and general errors
4. Added timeout to requests.get to prevent hanging
5. Added response status code checking with raise_for_status()
6. Removed hardcoded domain and uses the actual domain from handle
7. Added docstring comment
8. Structured error handling with specific exception types

The code now properly handles various error cases while maintaining the original functionality of retrieving and parsing Diaspora webfinger documents.

